{"parentUuid":"3b53ddd6-1b20-45fc-b623-23b7c1230916","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14950028 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9b72da51-5923-413b-b363-199f71435d6a","timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:37:52.179Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14950028 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"5b2f51a7-c436-4470-a434-c0a3f65ff73c","snapshotMessageId":"793b6dfd-8117-422b-92cb-bd6c905cb655","trackingPath":"docs/architecture/07-pm-workflow.md","backup":{"backupFileName":"ce0df64139dd7671@v1","version":1,"backupTime":"2026-10-10T19:38:05.423Z","realParentDir":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture"},"timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:38:05.423Z"}
{"parentUuid":"9b72da51-5923-413b-b363-199f71435d6a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu7yw2FVqhDNg95fYFkp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017UgWFNVgaQxCH7cTRrAX6U","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/07-pm-workflow.md","content":"# Product manager workflow\n\nThe product manager's path: market → series → AI analysis (customer feedback, plus a research agent for competitors and trends) → one list where the PM keeps, rejects (with a required reason), reorders priority and wishlists competitor/trend features → build car profiles that follow that priority → optional social test (L3).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  %% The product manager's path through Dixi, screen by screen. Implemented in web/: /dashboard/[market]/[series].\n  %% Layers: L1 = BMW principles · L2 = customer feedback + competitors + trends · L3 = social response to the profiles (low weight).\n  %% Every reject asks for a reason; the reason is saved as a decision and shown on the profiles.\n  %% The PM's priority order is a human input: profiles pick and list requests in that order.\n\n  landing[\"Landing page\"] --> picker[\"Dashboard<br/>globe: pick a market\"]\n  picker --> series[\"Pick a series<br/>1 · 5 · 7\"]\n  series --> analyse\n\n  subgraph analyse [\"AI analysis\"]\n    direction TB\n    l2in[\"L2 · Customer feedback<br/>likes · dislikes · wishes\"]\n    research[\"L2 · Research agent<br/>competitor features people like<br/>+ market trends, with sources\"]\n    cluster[\"Compress + cluster<br/>into feature requests\"]\n    cat[\"Categorise<br/>Exterior · Interior · Digital · Powertrain\"]\n    urgency[\"Urgency<br/>how many customers ask for it\"]\n    link[\"Link feedback ↔ competitors / trends<br/>matching requests get highlighted\"]\n    l2in --> cluster --> cat --> urgency --> link\n    research --> link\n  end\n\n  link --> list[\"One list<br/>competitors &amp; trends on top · customer requests below<br/>filter: category · urgency · backed by market\"]\n\n  list --> pick{{\"PM decides per request\"}}\n  pick -- \"Keep\" --> kept[\"Kept requests\"]\n  pick -- \"Reject\" --> why[\"Reason box<br/>why is it rejected?<br/>(required)\"]\n  list -- \"Drag to reorder\" --> prio[\"Priority order<br/>#1, #2, #3 …\"]\n  list -- \"Star a competitor feature or trend\" --> wish[\"Wishlist<br/>not asked for by customers yet\"]\n\n  why --> mem[(\"Decisions<br/>keep · reject + reason · wishlist<br/>who · when\")]\n  kept --> mem\n  wish --> mem\n\n  kept --> build[\"Build\"]\n  prio -- \"picks + orders requirements\" --> build\n  wish -- \"added where the profile's theme fits\" --> build\n  l1[\"L1 · BMW principles<br/>per series\"] --> build\n  mem -. \"rejected requests stay out\" .-> build\n  build --> profiles[\"3 car profiles<br/>Fix the basics · Tech-forward · Comfort &amp; craft<br/>score = L1 (principles + your priority) + L2 coverage\"]\n\n  profiles --> page[\"Profile page<br/>requirements in your priority order · draft targets<br/>related options + price · competitors &amp; trends<br/>why the agent chose it · Decisions incl. reject reasons\"]\n  mem --> page\n\n  page -. \"optional\" .-> post[\"Post the profiles on social media\"]\n  post --> l3[\"L3 · Which profile performs better<br/>low weight per series\"]\n  l3 --> dash[\"Dashboard<br/>profile scores per market\"]\n  page --> dash\n\n  classDef screen fill:#ffffff,stroke:#1c69d4,color:#121722\n  classDef ai fill:#e8f0fc,stroke:#1c69d4,color:#121722\n  classDef human fill:#fdecea,stroke:#e22718,color:#121722,stroke-width:2px\n  classDef memory fill:#0f3d75,stroke:#0f3d75,color:#ffffff\n  classDef layer fill:#eef1f6,stroke:#5b6676,color:#121722\n\n  class landing,picker,series,list,page,dash screen\n  class cluster,cat,urgency,link,build,profiles ai\n  class pick,why,kept,prio,wish human\n  class mem memory\n  class l1,l2in,research,l3,post layer\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1413,"cache_read_input_tokens":251456,"output_tokens":2241,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1413,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2241,"cache_read_input_tokens":251456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1413},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017UgWFNVgaQxCH7cTRrAX6U":{"file_path":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/07-pm-workflow.md","content":"# Product manager workflow\n\nThe product manager's path: market → series → AI analysis (customer feedback, plus a research agent for competitors and trends) → one list where the PM keeps, rejects (with a required reason), reorders priority and wishlists competitor/trend features → build car profiles that follow that priority → optional social test (L3).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  %% The product manager's path through Dixi, screen by screen. Implemented in web/: /dashboard/[market]/[series].\n  %% Layers: L1 = BMW principles · L2 = customer feedback + competitors + trends · L3 = social response to the profiles (low weight).\n  %% Every reject asks for a reason; the reason is saved as a decision and shown on the profiles.\n  %% The PM's priority order is a human input: profiles pick and list requests in that order.\n\n  landing[\"Landing page\"] --> picker[\"Dashboard<br/>globe: pick a market\"]\n  picker --> series[\"Pick a series<br/>1 · 5 · 7\"]\n  series --> analyse\n\n  subgraph analyse [\"AI analysis\"]\n    direction TB\n    l2in[\"L2 · Customer feedback<br/>likes · dislikes · wishes\"]\n    research[\"L2 · Research agent<br/>competitor features people like<br/>+ market trends, with sources\"]\n    cluster[\"Compress + cluster<br/>into feature requests\"]\n    cat[\"Categorise<br/>Exterior · Interior · Digital · Powertrain\"]\n    urgency[\"Urgency<br/>how many customers ask for it\"]\n    link[\"Link feedback ↔ competitors / trends<br/>matching requests get highlighted\"]\n    l2in --> cluster --> cat --> urgency --> link\n    research --> link\n  end\n\n  link --> list[\"One list<br/>competitors &amp; trends on top · customer requests below<br/>filter: category · urgency · backed by market\"]\n\n  list --> pick{{\"PM decides per request\"}}\n  pick -- \"Keep\" --> kept[\"Kept requests\"]\n  pick -- \"Reject\" --> why[\"Reason box<br/>why is it rejected?<br/>(required)\"]\n  list -- \"Drag to reorder\" --> prio[\"Priority order<br/>#1, #2, #3 …\"]\n  list -- \"Star a competitor feature or trend\" --> wish[\"Wishlist<br/>not asked for by customers yet\"]\n\n  why --> mem[(\"Decisions<br/>keep · reject + reason · wishlist<br/>who · when\")]\n  kept --> mem\n  wish --> mem\n\n  kept --> build[\"Build\"]\n  prio -- \"picks + orders requirements\" --> build\n  wish -- \"added where the profile's theme fits\" --> build\n  l1[\"L1 · BMW principles<br/>per series\"] --> build\n  mem -. \"rejected requests stay out\" .-> build\n  build --> profiles[\"3 car profiles<br/>Fix the basics · Tech-forward · Comfort &amp; craft<br/>score = L1 (principles + your priority) + L2 coverage\"]\n\n  profiles --> page[\"Profile page<br/>requirements in your priority order · draft targets<br/>related options + price · competitors &amp; trends<br/>why the agent chose it · Decisions incl. reject reasons\"]\n  mem --> page\n\n  page -. \"optional\" .-> post[\"Post the profiles on social media\"]\n  post --> l3[\"L3 · Which profile performs better<br/>low weight per series\"]\n  l3 --> dash[\"Dashboard<br/>profile scores per market\"]\n  page --> dash\n\n  classDef screen fill:#ffffff,stroke:#1c69d4,color:#121722\n  classDef ai fill:#e8f0fc,stroke:#1c69d4,color:#121722\n  classDef human fill:#fdecea,stroke:#e22718,color:#121722,stroke-width:2px\n  classDef memory fill:#0f3d75,stroke:#0f3d75,color:#ffffff\n  classDef layer fill:#eef1f6,stroke:#5b6676,color:#121722\n\n  class landing,picker,series,list,page,dash screen\n  class cluster,cat,urgency,link,build,profiles ai\n  class pick,why,kept,prio,wish human\n  class mem memory\n  class l1,l2in,research,l3,post layer\n```\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfu7yviPNjBdwsfk8tXTq","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b2f51a7-c436-4470-a434-c0a3f65ff73c","timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:38:05.387Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
