{"parentUuid":"3d54c8b6-3f81-4078-92a7-c06dabeeb6ff","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d96a1aea-49b1-48de-a7fd-354623c22deb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HTqyFq3dMwJTqBC9rDtNKf","type":"tool_result","content":"no console errors","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c7e9ee2d-2bea-471e-81d1-3f2f2a74da5e","timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:38:17.120Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"no console errors","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":7,"newStart":13,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | [`04-build-plan.md`](architecture/04-build-plan.md) | The hackathon build plan, prioritised by the judging criteria |"," | [`05-hitl-map.md`](architecture/05-hitl-map.md) | Where the human sits in the pipeline, and why |"," | [`06-web-app.md`](architecture/06-web-app.md) | The current Next.js app: routes, components, shared globe, data modules, planned backend |","-| [`07-pm-workflow.md`](architecture/07-pm-workflow.md) | The product manager's path: market → series → AI clusters feature requests (Exterior · Interior · Digital · Powertrain, by urgency) → keep or reject (a reject needs a reason, saved in Decisions) → build car profiles → optional social test (L3) |","+| [`07-pm-workflow.md`](architecture/07-pm-workflow.md) | The product manager's path, as built in `/dashboard/[market]/[series]`: market → series → AI analysis + research agent (competitors, trends) → keep / reject with a required reason / reorder priority / wishlist → profiles that follow the PM's priority → optional social test (L3) |"," "," ## Core ideas in one paragraph"," Dixi turns customer feedback from every market into requirements for the next BMW, and keeps the reason for every decision. Signals sit in three layers: **L1 principles** (hard rules per market, owned by people), **L2 evidence** (customer studies, owner feedback, sales, quality data) and **L3 signals** (social media, search trends, concept tests). Each model has its own weights: social signals count more for an entry model than for a flagship. AI drafts most requirements as SMART targets; a product manager keeps, edits, postpones or rejects each one at defined gates. Every decision is stored with its evidence snapshot, so anyone can trace a requirement back to the comments behind it. Dixi also shows what it doesn't know: missing markets, thin samples and conflicting signals."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/README.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3d54c8b6-3f81-4078-92a7-c06dabeeb6ff","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
