{"parentUuid":"16e956a5-8382-450a-af7e-1439ea41602b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu91rYHadrrQh5TYVRmj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2956,"cache_read_input_tokens":351545,"output_tokens":1108,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":140},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2956,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1108,"cache_read_input_tokens":351545,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2956,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2956},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7888,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfu91qoPkMhPvHoUx8AeG","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"dataviz","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5a56469-43e2-4b6d-99b7-6105df8b470b","timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:51:33.967Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"c5a56469-43e2-4b6d-99b7-6105df8b470b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu91rYHadrrQh5TYVRmj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've redone the page header, added feedback when you move rows, and made **Build profiles** end the pipeline in a profiles dashboard with Profiles and Analytics tabs. I clicked through the whole flow in a headless browser with no errors, and the profile page exports as a clean 3-page A4 PDF. Reload with **Cmd+Shift+R**: the dev server had been serving old styles, so I cleared its cache and restarted it.\n\n**Header and photos**\n- The top of the page is now a dark banner. The car photo fills the right side and fades into navy behind the text.\n- It shows three stat chips: customer comments, feature requests, and competitors & trends.\n- The photo credit is smaller but still visible and linked, as the photo licence requires.\n- The profile page uses the same banner with the second photo (rear or interior).\n\n**Moving rows in the list**\n- While you drag, the row you're moving dims and gets a dashed outline.\n- A blue line with a dot shows where the row will land, above or below the row under your cursor.\n- The other rows slide smoothly into their new places.\n- The row you moved flashes blue for about a second. This also works when you move it with ↑ ↓.\n\n**When the build is done**\n- The pipeline is marked complete and you land on the **Profiles dashboard**.\n- **Profiles tab:** three cards, each with its score bar, its requirements with category icons and your priority numbers, and its wishlist items.\n- **Analytics tab:** you launch a 14-day social test.\n  - **Leader:** a card names the profile tracking best, with its lead in points.\n  - **Per profile:** reach, engagement, positive reactions and a week-2-vs-week-1 trend.\n  - **Chart:** daily engagement per profile, with hover details and a table view. Each profile keeps the same colour everywhere, and the colours were checked for colour-blind readers.\n- The test result also updates each profile's score, at the small social weight for that series.\n- **The social test is simulated**, and the page says so. There are no real posts behind it yet.\n\n**Profile page**\n- From top to bottom:\n  1. The banner.\n  2. Four key numbers: requirements, customer mentions covered, today's option prices, and wishlist items.\n  3. The requirements in your priority order, each with a draft target and the related options.\n  4. Why the agent chose this profile, next to the L1 principles.\n  5. Competitors & trends, with their sources.\n  6. The decision trail, including reject reasons.\n  7. A short line on where the evidence comes from.\n- **Download PDF** opens the print dialog; choose \"Save as PDF\". The navigation is left out, and the report gets its own header with the series, market, profile and date.\n\nThe architecture diagram `docs/architecture/07-pm-workflow.md` now covers the dashboard, both tabs and the PDF, and it renders without errors.\n\nStill waiting on you: **three markets (Europe, China, USA), or the UK instead of Japan?**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2956,"cache_read_input_tokens":351545,"output_tokens":1108,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":140},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2956,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1108,"cache_read_input_tokens":351545,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2956,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2956},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfu91qoPkMhPvHoUx8AeG",