{"parentUuid":"29297486-2e6d-459d-b01e-15c0e9667af6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu9n8cf5mDZxTFSWQSqA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. I tested it with real mouse events: dragging row 5, \"More comfortable, better-equipped seats\", up the list moved it to position 2, and the rows below moved down by one. No console errors, and types and lint pass.\n\n**Cause:** the list used the browser's built-in drag-and-drop on the handle button. In Chrome, the page re-rendering at the start of the drag can cancel it, so rows didn't move. I replaced it with my own pointer-based dragging, which also works with a trackpad and on touch screens.\n\n**How it works now:**\n- Press and hold the **⋮⋮ handle** (left of the number) and drag. The row lifts with a blue outline and shadow and follows your cursor.\n- A blue line shows where it will land.\n- Near the top or bottom of the window the page scrolls by itself, so you can move a row a long way.\n- On release, the rows slide into place, the moved row flashes, and the new order is saved and used for the profiles.\n- Keyboard still works: click the handle, then use ↑ ↓.\n\nReload the page to get the fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1913,"cache_read_input_tokens":402356,"output_tokens":430,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":79},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1913,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":402356,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1913},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"co