{"parentUuid":"fd081f9d-81b2-41b4-bbe7-2dd76f674014","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14939322 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e6e39507-9bf1-4d49-91c8-26f1572a31b0","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:12:05.284Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14939322 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"e6e39507-9bf1-4d49-91c8-26f1572a31b0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01691S6LmoyJwSi4VW8wn8S4","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"43a1935c-9e6d-4b8b-9841-7f9efe36832d","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:12:17.109Z","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"43a1935c-9e6d-4b8b-9841-7f9efe36832d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuAbH6CEdV1TMSaNSdVW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I did all three: the profile page now follows BMW's catalogue layout, the profile cards match the series cards, and every build is saved as a session you can reopen. I tested build → profile → Sessions page → reopen in a headless browser with no errors, and types pass. Reload with **Cmd+Shift+R**.\n\n**What I took from BMW's catalogues** (5, 1 and 7 Series, July 2026):\n- **Cover:** a full-bleed photo with a big light \"BMW 5 / LIMOUSINE\" title and the month at the bottom.\n- **Section titles:** uppercase with a full stop, like \"FAHRZEUGPREISE.\" and \"SONDERAUSSTATTUNGEN.\".\n- **Tables:** grey band headers and hairline rules.\n- **Equipment matrix:** model columns with turned headers, ■ for standard and □ for optional, plus option code and price written like \"1.900,–\".\n- **Legend:** a short key at the foot of every page.\n\n**The profile page now follows that layout:**\n1. **Cover:** the car photo with \"BMW 5\" in large light type, \"PROFILE A · COMFORT & CRAFT\", the tagline, and market · month · session at the bottom.\n2. **PROFILE AT A GLANCE.** Two tables with grey bands: Score (L1, L2, L3, total) and Scope (series, requirements, customer mentions covered, wishlist, total price of related options).\n3. **REQUIREMENTS.** The catalogue matrix:\n   - Grouped by Exterior, Interior, Digital, Powertrain and Wishlist, in your priority order (#1, #2…).\n   - Each row has its draft target, plus the option code and its list price where an option matches.\n   - One column per profile shows ■ in this profile, □ in another profile, or – not included, so you can compare all three at once.\n4. **WHY THIS PROFILE.** and **PRINCIPLES.** side by side.\n5. **COMPETITORS AND TRENDS.** with source links.\n6. **DECISION TRAIL.** with reject reasons, who and when.\n7. **Legend and evidence note** at the foot, as in BMW's lists.\n\nDownload PDF still prints this layout to A4.\n\n**Profile cards:** these are now dark cards like the series picker:\n- The car photo is tinted in each profile's colour, with a \"PROFILE A\" badge and a white \"Best fit\" badge on the winner.\n- Below it: the name, a score bar, the top requirements with category icons and priority numbers, any wishlist items, and a white \"Open profile\" button.\n\n**Sessions:**\n- Every **Build profiles** saves a session: its profiles, decisions, priority order and social test results. They're kept in your browser for now, up to the last 30.\n- **Three ways in:**\n  - A **Sessions** link in the top bar, on every dashboard page.\n  - A **Sessions** item in the dashboard sidebar. Sessions for this car and market open in place; others take you to their own page.\n  - A link per session (`…/5-series#session=S-…`) that reopens it directly.\n- The dashboard header shows which session you're looking at.\n- **Edit requests** loads that session's decisions, and building again creates a new session.\n\nI also updated `docs/architecture/07-pm-workflow.md` with sessions and the catalogue-style profile page. It renders without errors.\n\nStill open:\n- **Storage:** sessions only live in your browser until we connect Supabase.\n- **Markets:** still waiting on your answer: three markets (Europe, China, USA), or the UK instead of Japan?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":545,"cache_read_input_tokens":465840,"output_tokens":1183,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":545,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":465840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":545},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuAbGcAzFLrxpee1krc2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2754380-4b5a-47cf-b860-95dd3912e87d","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:12:17.106Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
