{"parentUuid":"bbd5e05a-b0ce-4171-833f-c8590a378f8c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuB9cjnNjRDTvFXxqsGj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll split this up. One agent rebuilds the landing page and another updates the architecture docs, while I do the single button and the decision author myself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3711,"cache_read_input_tokens":512155,"output_tokens":4901,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":262},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3711,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4901,"cache_read_input_tokens":512155,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3711},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfuB9cLiVkGXNXmnfywp7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"be661d90-95cc-4c8e-858a-ee186ace2db5","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:19:28.918Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"be661d90-95cc-4c8e-858a-ee186ace2db5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuB9cjnNjRDTvFXxqsGj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016S2EFh3UoDRDJPEZ99dwyF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Redesign landing for new workflow","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Improve the landing page of the Dixi web app (Next.js 16, React 19, Tailwind 4) so it explains the product's NEW workflow and uses the real car photos. The repo is /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026 and the app is in web/.\n\nRead first:\n- web/AGENTS.md: Next 16 has breaking changes. Check web/node_modules/next/dist/docs/ before using an unfamiliar API.\n- AGENTS.md at the repo root: rules. In particular, no real BMW data, numbers or customer quotes on the landing page (it's deployed publicly), no AI attribution anywhere, and no git commands.\n- web/src/app/globals.css: colour tokens. Use the Tailwind token names (bg-ink, text-brand, bg-brand-soft, bg-l1/l2/l3, text-muted, ring-line, shadow-card, shadow-float, rounded-card…), never raw hex.\n- Current landing: web/src/app/page.tsx, web/src/components/landing/{Hero,Process,LayerWeights,Product,ProductMock}.tsx, web/src/components/site/{Navbar,Footer,ButtonLink}.tsx.\n- The look and feel of the app the landing should match: web/src/components/pipeline/SeriesPicker.tsx (dark navy photo cards), CarBanner.tsx (dark banner with the photo fading into navy), Profiles.tsx (catalogue-style profile page with uppercase \"TITLE.\" headings and ■/□ matrix), and docs/architecture/07-pm-workflow.md (the workflow).\n- web/src/lib/car-images.ts: CC BY-SA photos of the F70 / G60 / G70. Every photo shown must show its credit and link to its Commons page, marked \"modified\".\n\nThe new workflow and mental model (use these words; keep copy short and plain, no jargon):\n1. **Pick a market** on the globe (Europe, China, USA…).\n2. **Pick the car**: 1 Series, 5 Series or 7 Series.\n3. **AI analysis**:\n   - **BMW principles**: the fundamentals the car must respect (owned by managers).\n   - **Market evidence**: customer feedback and feature requests, customer studies, sales, today's option list, plus a research agent that scans competitors and market trends with sources.\n   - Similar comments are grouped into **feature requests**, sorted into Exterior · Interior · Digital · Powertrain, with urgency (how many customers ask).\n4. **The product manager decides**:\n   - Keep or reject each request. A reject always needs a written reason.\n   - Drag to set priority.\n   - Star competitor features or trends onto a wishlist.\n   - Every decision records who made it and when.\n5. **Build profiles**: 2–3 car profiles (e.g. \"Fix the basics\", \"Tech-forward\", \"Comfort & craft\"). Each follows the PM's priority and BMW's principles, explains why the agent chose it, and exports a catalogue-style PDF.\n6. **Social test (after the profiles exist)**: post the profiles and see which one tracks better. It's a small-weight tie-breaker.\n7. **Generations**: every build is saved; the dashboard lists earlier generations to reopen, compare or rebuild.\n\nLayers (update LayerWeights accordingly):\n- **L1 BMW principles.**\n- **L2 Market evidence**: customers, competitors and trends.\n- **L3 Social test** on the generated profiles, with low weight per model (7 Series ≈ 2 %, 5 Series ≈ 8 %, 1 Series ≈ 20 %).\n\nRemove the old \"Japan multi-storey car park\" example from the copy. Use a neutral example such as \"the 7 Series puts rear-seat comfort first\".\n\nWhat to build (keep the existing Hero globe and its popping comments untouched, apart from optional small copy tweaks that match the new concept):\n- **Process section:** a clear, visual version of the workflow above. For example a numbered horizontal or vertical flow of 6–7 steps with lucide icons, where the \"PM decides\" step is highlighted in the human-decision red (text-human / bg-human-soft) as the human gate. Keep it scannable.\n- **\"Choose the car\" section:** the 3 series as dark navy photo cards, like SeriesPicker (photo, model code chip, name, one-line positioning). Each links to /dashboard/new. Credits visible and linked, small.\n- **Product section:** replace or refresh the ProductMock so it reflects the real app. Either a CSS mock of a profile catalogue page (cover with car photo + \"BMW 5 · PROFILE A · COMFORT & CRAFT\", a small requirements matrix with ■ □) or a mock of the generations dashboard. Keep the existing AI-generated product image only if it still fits, and keep its \"AI-generated image\" label (EU AI Act). Update the three feature bullets to: Traceable decisions (who, when, why) · Competitors & trends with sources · Generations you can reopen and export as PDF.\n- **Navbar:** links Process / Cars / Product / Contact, plus the \"Open dashboard\" button.\n- Make sure the page works at phone width (no horizontal scroll), respects prefers-reduced-motion, and keeps good contrast.\n\nChecks you must run:\n- `cd /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web && pnpm exec tsc --noEmit && pnpm lint`. Fix all errors and warnings in files you touched.\n- A dev server is already running on http://localhost:3000; don't start another. Take screenshots of http://localhost:3000/ at 1440×900 (full page) and 390×844 with headless Chrome, using the helper `node /Volumes/PJ/DevCache/claude-tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-PJ-peresjav-hackathons-ehl-final-minuch-2026/7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1/scratchpad/cdp-shot.mjs <url> <out.png> <width> <height> <waitMs>`. Use a large height for a full-page view. Save the images in that scratchpad folder, look at them, and fix layout problems.\n- Only touch files under web/src/components/landing/, web/src/components/site/Navbar.tsx, web/src/app/page.tsx and, if needed, new files in web/src/components/landing/. Don't touch the dashboard or pipeline components, globals.css or the docs.\n\nReport back with the files changed, a short description of each new section, and the screenshot paths.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3711,"cache_read_input_tokens":512155,"output_tokens":4901,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":262},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3711,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4901,"cache_read_input_tokens":512155,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3711},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016S2EFh3UoDRDJPEZ99dwyF":{"description":"Redesign landing for new workflow","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Improve the landing page of the Dixi web app (Next.js 16, React 19, Tailwind 4) so it explains the product's NEW workflow and uses the real car photos. The repo is /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026 and the app is in web/.\n\nRead first:\n- web/AGENTS.md: Next 16 has breaking changes. Check web/node_modules/next/dist/docs/ before using an unfamiliar API.\n- AGENTS.md at the repo root: rules. In particular, no real BMW data, numbers or customer quotes on the landing page (it's deployed publicly), no AI attribution anywhere, and no git commands.\n- web/src/app/globals.css: colour tokens. Use the Tailwind token names (bg-ink, text-brand, bg-brand-soft, bg-l1/l2/l3, text-muted, ring-line, shadow-card, shadow-float, rounded-card…), never raw hex.\n- Current landing: web/src/app/page.tsx, web/src/components/landing/{Hero,Process,LayerWeights,Product,ProductMock}.tsx, web/src/components/s