 AI analysis (BMW principles → market evidence → building the list).\n   - Feature requests by category (Exterior / Interior / Digital / Powertrain) and urgency.\n   - PM keeps or rejects, with a required reason; drags to set priority; stars competitor/trend signals onto a wishlist.\n   - Build → 3 profiles (Fix the basics / Tech-forward / Comfort & craft). They follow the PM's priority; the score is L1 (principles + priority) + L2 coverage.\n   - Each build is saved as a **generation** → /dashboard/generations#id with Profiles, Analytics (L3 social test, simulated), Decisions, and \"Edit and rebuild\".\n   - The profile page is in the style of BMW's option-list catalogue (■/□ matrix vs the other profiles) and exports a PDF via print.\n3. **Decisions record who and when.** Each decision stores `by` (the PM's name, from a simple local \"who's deciding\" identity until there's a login) and `at` (ISO timestamp). Reject reasons are mandatory.\n4. **Storage today:** decisions, priority and generations are in localStorage. The BMW-derived data is in web/data-local/pipeline.json (git-ignored), built by scripts/build-pipeline-data.py; otherwise example data is used (Vercel). Planned: Supabase tables.\n\nDeliverables:\n- **README.md:** update the three-layer table (L1 BMW principles / L2 market evidence / L3 social test) and the \"five steps\" list and mermaid to match the workflow above, still simple and short. Keep the badges, live link and structure.\n- **docs/README.md:** update the \"Core ideas in one paragraph\" and the file table (07 already listed).\n- **docs/architecture/01-system-overview.md:** update the mermaid to the new layer definitions and workflow: research agent → L2, PM gate with keep / reject reason / priority / wishlist, profiles, generations, social test as L3 after profiles. Keep the classDef colour conventions already in the file.\n- **docs/architecture/03-data-model.md:** update the ER diagram to the real entities: SERIES, MARKET, FEATURE_REQUEST (category, urgency, mentions by market, taxonomy, quotes), OPTION_ITEM, MARKET_SIGNAL (competitor | trend, sources, relates_to requests), PRINCIPLE, DECISION (keep | reject | wish, reason, by, at), GENERATION (session: profiles, decisions, priority order, campaigns, created_at, created_by), PROFILE, PROFILE_REQUIREMENT (priority, draft target), CAMPAIGN (L3 social test per profile). Mark what's in localStorage today vs planned Supabase in a short note above the diagram.\n- **docs/architecture/08-decision-audit.md (new):** a short sequence diagram showing how a decision is made and audited: PM → reject → reason dialog (required) → Decision {by, at, reason} → saved → shown in the decision log, the profile's decision trail and the PDF → new generation keeps a snapshot. Add a row for it to docs/README.md's table.\n- Leave 02, 04, 05 as they are unless something in them is now flatly wrong (then fix that minimally and say so).\n\nValidate every Mermaid diagram you touched by rendering it in headless Chrome. There's a helper at `/Volumes/PJ/DevCache/claude-tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-PJ-peresjav-hackathons-ehl-final-minuch-2026/7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1/scratchpad/cdp-eval.mjs <url> \"<js expr>\" <times> <gapMs>`. The template is the HTML file /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/reports/pm-workflow.html: it loads mermaid 11.4.1 from jsdelivr, renders `<pre class=\"mermaid\">`, sets document.title to \"OK\" on success and writes errors into #err. Copy it to the scratchpad per diagram, replace the pre content (HTML-escaped), open it as file://…, and evaluate `document.title+' '+document.getElementById('err').textContent`. It must print \"OK\". Don't modify reports/pm-workflow.html itself.\n\nReport back with the files changed, one line per change, and the validation results.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creati