{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:24:30.408Z","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a88d534d736d09bb2</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_016S2EFh3UoDRDJPEZ99dwyF</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/Volumes/PJ/DevCache/claude-tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-PJ-peresjav-hackathons-ehl-final-minuch-2026/53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46/tasks/a88d534d736d09bb2.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Redesign landing for new workflow\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I've rebuilt the landing page around the new workflow and the real car photos. `tsc --noEmit` and `pnpm lint` both pass with no errors or warnings. I checked the page in screenshots at 1440 and 390 wide and fixed what looked wrong. At 390 nothing looked wider than the screen, but I didn't measure the page width with a script.\n\n**New sections, in page order:**\n- **Process (`#process`):** a vertical numbered timeline of the 7 steps, each with a lucide icon. On desktop the heading on the left stays in place while you scroll the steps. Step 3 (AI analysis) shows BMW principles and Market evidence as two tinted boxes, plus the grouping into feature requests with Exterior · Interior · Digital · Powertrain chips. Step 4 (PM decides) is the only red step, with a \"Human gate\" badge and the four decision rules. A small key at the top explains \"AI step\" vs \"Human gate\".\n- **Layers box (below the timeline):** L1 BMW principles (with the \"7 Series puts rear-seat comfort first\" example), L2 Market evidence, L3 Social test. It shows a weight bar for each of the three series: L3 is 2 %, 8 % and 20 %, and L1 takes 45 % of the rest, the same split the pipeline code uses. It's labelled as illustrative defaults.\n- **Choose the car (`#cars`):** three dark navy photo cards in the same style as the dashboard's series picker: photo, model code chip (F70 / G60 / G70), name, one-line positioning, a \"Social test weight\" chip and a \"Start analysis\" button. All three link to `/dashboard/new`. Below them is a small credit line linking each photo to its Commons page, marked \"modified (resized)\".\n- **Product (`#product`):** new headline and intro copy, and a new coded mock.\n  - **Catalogue page:** the 5 Series cover with \"BMW 5 · PROFILE A · COMFORT &amp; CRAFT\" and the photo credit linked and marked \"modified\". Below it, a \"REQUIREMENTS.\" table with Interior and Digital groups and ■ □ – marks across profiles A, B and C.\n  - **Side panel:** a Generations list with Reopen / Compare / Rebuild, a rejected request with its written reason, who and when, and a Download PDF button.\n  - **AI image and bullets:** I kept the AI-generated laptop image (a globe and a ranked list, so it still fits) with its \"AI-generated image\" label. The three bullets are now Traceable decisions · Competitors &amp; trends with sources · Generations you can reopen.\n- **Navbar:** Process / Cars / Product / Contact, plus Open dashboard.\n- **Hero:** the globe and popping comments are untouched. Only the intro sentence and the page meta description were changed to describe the new flow.\n\nThe \"Japan multi-storey car park\" example is gone. All mock content is invented, with no BMW data, numbers or customer quotes. Every hover effect is switched off under prefers-reduced-motion, and colours use only the token names.\n\n**Files changed** (under `/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web/src/`):\n- `components/landing/Process.tsx` (rewritten)\n- `components/landing/LayerWeights.tsx` (rewritten)\n- `components/landing/Cars.tsx` (new)\n- `components/landing/ProductMock.tsx` (rewritten)\n- `components/landing/Product.tsx`\n- `components/landing/Hero.tsx`\n- `components/site/Navbar.tsx`\n- `app/page.tsx`\n\n**Screenshots** are in `/Volumes/PJ/DevCache/claude-tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-PJ-peresjav-hackathons-ehl-final-minuch-2026/7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1/scratchpad/`:\n- `landing-1440.png`: full page, 1440 wide\n- `landing-390.png`: full page, 390 wide\n- `landing-390-viewport.png`: 390×844 viewport\n- `d0.png` to `d3.png`, `d-fix.png`, `d-mock.png` (desktop) and `m0.png` to `m3.png` (phone): slices for easier viewing\n\nThe footer still links only Process / Product / Dashboard, because it was outside the files I was allowed to change. Adding \"Cars\" there is a one-line change in `components/site/Footer.tsx` if you want it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>133360</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>28</tool_uses><duration_ms>278570</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
