{"parentUuid":"1e67a390-ddc1-414f-ba5b-3243bdbfc691","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"55e0a9c9-5e46-447d-bd51-556d6261cceb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XkLtLiSCJq8gVxvent3N7U","type":"tool_result","content":"1\nOK\n# Dixi backend (planned)\n\nNot built yet. This folder will hold the API and the AI agents behind the dashboard. Today the web app runs on typed sample data in `web/src/lib/`.\n\n## Planned stack\nPython · **FastAPI** · **Pydantic AI** (agents with typed outputs) · **Supabase** (Postgres + pgvector) · **OpenAI**. Details and alternatives: `../docs/tech-stack/README.md`. Architecture: `../docs/architecture/`.\n\n## Planned layout\n```\nbackend/\n├── app/\n│   ├── main.py              FastAPI app, routes\n│   ├── api/                 /markets, /requirements, /decisions, /lineage, /weights, /principles, /gaps\n│   ├── agents/              labeller, clusterer, requirement writer, prioritiser, scribe (Pydantic AI)\n│   ├── scoring/             three-layer score: layer weights × source weights × market volume, principle gate\n│   ├── models/              Pydantic data contracts (Evidence, Requirement, Decision, Principle, Gap, …)\n│   └── db/                  Supabase client, migrations\n├── tests/\n└── pyproject.toml           managed with uv\n```\n\n## Rules\n- Customer data is never committed. Load it from Supabase or a local, git-ignored folder.\n- Secrets come from the repo-root `.env` (git-ignored).\n- Every agent output is typed and stored with its inputs, so each requirement can be traced back to its evidence.\n18:  FEATURE_REQUEST ||--o| DECISION : \"keep or reject\"\n19:  MARKET_SIGNAL ||--o| DECISION : \"wish\"\n20-  GENERATION }o--|| SERIES : \"for\"\n21-  GENERATION }o--|| MARKET : \"scope\"\n22:  GENERATION ||--o{ DECISION : \"snapshot of\"\n23-  GENERATION ||--|{ PROFILE : \"builds 3\"\n24-  PROFILE ||--o{ PROFILE_REQUIREMENT : \"lists, in PM order\"\n25-  FEATURE_REQUEST ||--o{ PROFILE_REQUIREMENT : \"becomes\"\n26-  PROFILE }o--o{ MARKET_SIGNAL : \"wishes · backing\"\n27-  GENERATION ||--o{ CAMPAIGN : \"L3 social test\"\n28-  PROFILE ||--o| CAMPAIGN : \"tracked by\"\n29-\n30-  SERIES { text id \"F70 | G60 | G70\" text name text slug text focus \"categories\" float l3_weight \"0.20 | 0.08 | 0.02\" }\n31-  MARKET { text id \"EU | US | CN | JP | ALL\" text name }\n32-  PRINCIPLE { text id \"P1\" text series_id text text text owner }\n33-  FEATURE_REQUEST { text id text series_id text title text category \"Exterior | Interior | Digital | Powertrain\" text summary int mentions jsonb by_market \"mentions per market\" jsonb types \"wants | difficult | defect\" jsonb sources text_array taxonomy \"BMW topics behind it\" text_array quotes \"local data only\" }\n34-  OPTION_ITEM { text code text name float price_eur text group }\n--\n36:  DECISION { text request_id text title text action \"keep | reject | wish\" text reason \"required for reject\" text by \"name, local identity\" text role timestamptz at }\n37-  GENERATION { text id \"G-...\" timestamptz created_at text created_by text created_by_role text scope text series_id jsonb profiles jsonb decisions text_array priority_order jsonb campaigns \"null until tested\" }\n38-  PROFILE { text id \"fix | tech | comfort\" text name text tagline text_array why float score_l1 float score_l2 float score_l3 \"null until tested\" float total }\n39-  PROFILE_REQUIREMENT { text profile_id text request_id int priority \"PM position, 1 = first\" int scoped_mentions text draft_target \"SMART draft, PM edits\" }\n40-  CAMPAIGN { text profile_id int days \"14\" int impressions float engagement float positive int shares float l3 \"0-1, simulated\" }\n41-```\n42-\n43-Urgency is not stored: it is derived from mentions in the chosen market (high ≥ 50, medium ≥ 20, else low). Draft targets are also derived (`draftTarget` in `profiles.ts`) when a profile is shown.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"411a4b95-45a5-4913-91a1-14534bb1e7c8","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:30:51.012Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1\nOK\n# Dixi backend (planned)\n\nNot built yet. This folder will hold the API and the AI agents behind the dashboard. Today the web app runs on typed sample data in `web/src/lib/`.\n\n## Planned stack\nPython · **FastAPI** · **Pydantic AI** (agents with typed outputs) · **Supabase** (Postgres + pgvector) · **OpenAI**. Details and alternatives: `../docs/tech-stack/README.md`. Architecture: `../docs/architecture/`.\n\n## Planned layout\n```\nbackend/\n├── app/\n│   ├── main.py              FastAPI app, routes\n│   ├── api/                 /markets, /requirements, /decisions, /lineage, /weights, /principles, /gaps\n│   ├── agents/              labeller, clusterer, requirement writer, prioritiser, scribe (Pydantic AI)\n│   ├── scoring/             three-layer score: layer weights × source weights × market volume, principle gate\n│   ├── models/              Pydantic data contracts (Evidence, Requirement, Decision, Principle, Gap, …)\n│   └── db/                  Supabase client, migrations\n├── tests/\n└── pyproject.toml           managed with uv\n```\n\n## Rules\n- Customer data is never committed. Load it from Supabase or a local, git-ignored folder.\n- Secrets come from the repo-root `.env` (git-ignored).\n- Every agent output is typed and stored with its inputs, so each requirement can be traced back to its evidence.\n18:  FEATURE_REQUEST ||--o| DECISION : \"keep or reject\"\n19:  MARKET_SIGNAL ||--o| DECISION : \"wish\"\n20-  GENERATION }o--|| SERIES : \"for\"\n21-  GENERATION }o--|| MARKET : \"scope\"\n22:  GENERATION ||--o{ DECISION : \"snapshot of\"\n23-  GENERATION ||--|{ PROFILE : \"builds 3\"\n24-  PROFILE ||--o{ PROFILE_REQUIREMENT : \"lists, in PM order\"\n25-  FEATURE_REQUEST ||--o{ PROFILE_REQUIREMENT : \"becomes\"\n26-  PROFILE }o--o{ MARKET_SIGNAL : \"wishes · backing\"\n27-  GENERATION ||--o{ CAMPAIGN : \"L3 social test\"\n28-  PROFILE ||--o| CAMPAIGN : \"tracked by\"\n29-\n30-  SERIES { text id \"F70 | G60 | G70\" text name text slug text focus \"categories\" float l3_weight \"0.20 | 0.08 | 0.02\" }\n31-  MARKET { text id \"EU | US | CN | JP | ALL\" text name }\n32-  PRINCIPLE { text id \"P1\" text series_id text text text owner }\n33-  FEATURE_REQUEST { text id text series_id text title text category \"Exterior | Interior | Digital | Powertrain\" text summary int mentions jsonb by_market \"mentions per market\" jsonb types \"wants | difficult | defect\" jsonb sources text_array taxonomy \"BMW topics behind it\" text_array quotes \"local data only\" }\n34-  OPTION_ITEM { text code text name float price_eur text group }\n--\n36:  DECISION { text request_id text title text action \"keep | reject | wish\" text reason \"required for reject\" text by \"name, local identity\" text role timestamptz at }\n37-  GENERATION { text id \"G-...\" timestamptz created_at text created_by text created_by_role text scope text series_id jsonb profiles jsonb decisions text_array priority_order jsonb campaigns \"null until tested\" }\n38-  PROFILE { text id \"fix | tech | comfort\" text name text tagline text_array why float score_l1 float score_l2 float score_l3 \"null until tested\" float total }\n39-  PROFILE_REQUIREMENT { text profile_id text request_id int priority \"PM position, 1 = first\" int scoped_mentions text draft_target \"SMART draft, PM edits\" }\n40-  CAMPAIGN { text profile_id int days \"14\" int impressions float engagement float positive int shares float l3 \"0-1, simulated\" }\n41-```\n42-\n43-Urgency is not stored: it is derived from mentions in the chosen market (high ≥ 50, medium ≥ 20, else low). Draft targets are also derived (`draftTarget` in `profiles.ts`) when a profile is shown.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web/src/components/dashboard/ScoringSettings.tsx","hunks":[{"oldStart":40,"oldLines":7,"newStart":40,"newLines