{"parentUuid":"dd07b1b4-f3fd-4f0a-9c18-e55238b25c9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuC2GDRAwNrT7YCxxAAj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the architecture: a new scoring-and-memory document, plus updates to the data model, workflow, docs index and backend plan."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2349,"cache_read_input_tokens":577203,"output_tokens":3285,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2349,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3285,"cache_read_input_tokens":577203,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2349},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuC2FjeXjC3je47znqNA","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3af9b539-49d2-420c-9374-3d89c0194ce5","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:30:52.750Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"3af9b539-49d2-420c-9374-3d89c0194ce5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuC2GDRAwNrT7YCxxAAj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A28SaADC9yjzwAjitSLcMi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md","content":"# Scoring and decision memory\n\nEvery decision (keep, reject with a reason, wishlist) is saved with **who** and **when**, together with how many customers asked at that moment. Later generations read this **decision memory**, so the AI does not push a request that was already rejected, unless the market has changed. The ranking rule and its weights are set by the team in **Dashboard → Settings** (`/dashboard/settings`).\n\n## The score (0–100, shown on every feature request)\n\n| Part | What it measures | Default weight |\n|---|---|---|\n| Demand | Customers asking in the chosen market, log-scaled against the top request | 60 % |\n| Market backing | Competitor features and trends (research agent) that support the request | 25 % |\n| Principle fit | The request's category matches the series' focus (BMW principles) | 15 % |\n\n```\nbase      = 100 × (wD·demand + wB·backing + wF·fit) / (wD + wB + wF)\nstrength  = 0.5 ^ (days since the decision / half-life)            default half-life 365 days\ngrowth    = (mentions now − mentions at decision) / mentions at decision\n\nrejected before:  score = base × (1 − penalty × strength)          default penalty 60 %\n   … unless growth ≥ resurface threshold → \"Resurfaced\", score = base   default +30 %\nkept before:      score = base + 10 × bonus × strength             default +5 points\noptional:         hide rejected requests instead of ranking them lower\nmemory scope:     same market (default) or all markets\n```\n\nThe PM's drag order always wins over the score. The score sets the default order and is shown so the PM can see why.\n\n## Flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  %% How past decisions shape the next generation.\n  classDef human fill:#fdecea,stroke:#e22718,color:#121722,stroke-width:2px\n  classDef store fill:#0f3d75,stroke:#0f3d75,color:#ffffff\n  classDef ai fill:#e8f0fc,stroke:#1c69d4,color:#121722\n  classDef cfg fill:#eef1f6,stroke:#5b6676,color:#121722\n\n  subgraph G1 [\"Generation 1\"]\n    pm1{{\"PM decides<br/>keep · reject + reason · wishlist\"}}:::human\n    d1[\"Decision<br/>by · role · at · reason · mentions_at\"]:::ai\n    pm1 --> d1\n  end\n\n  d1 --> mem[(\"Decision memory<br/>latest keep / reject per request<br/>(series + request; market or all)\")]:::store\n\n  subgraph G2 [\"Next generation\"]\n    reqs[\"New feature requests<br/>from fresh feedback + research\"]:::ai\n    match[\"Match to memory<br/>today: same series + title<br/>backend: + embedding similarity\"]:::ai\n    score[\"Dixi score<br/>demand · backing · fit<br/>× memory penalty / bonus\"]:::ai\n    list[\"Ranked list<br/>badges: Rejected · Resurfaced · Kept before\"]:::ai\n    pm2{{\"PM decides again<br/>sees the old reason, who and when\"}}:::human\n    reqs --> match --> score --> list --> pm2\n  end\n\n  mem --> match\n  settings[\"Settings<br/>weights · penalty · bonus · half-life<br/>resurface threshold · hide / rank lower\"]:::cfg --> score\n  pm2 --> mem\n```\n\n## Today vs backend\n\n| | Today (prototype, `web/`) | Backend (planned, `backend/`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Decisions | Saved with each generation in localStorage (`dixi:sessions`) | Table `decision` in Supabase, one row per decision, never overwritten |\n| Matching | Same series + same request title (`memoryKey`) | Same + pgvector similarity between a new cluster and past rejected requests, so a reworded request is still recognised |\n| Scoring | `web/src/lib/pipeline/scoring.ts` (`buildMemory`, `scoreRequest`) | Same rules in `backend/app/scoring/`, unit-tested against the web version |\n| Settings | `/dashboard/settings`, localStorage (`dixi:scoring`) | Table `scoring_settings` per team, with change history |\n| AI agent | Not involved yet: the list is built by a script | The requirement agent calls `get_decision_memory(series, market)` before it proposes requests. Rule in its instructions: *do not propose a rejected request again unless it resurfaced; when you do, quote the old reason and show the demand change.* |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2349,"cache_read_input_tokens":577203,"output_tokens":3285,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2349,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3285,"cache_read_input_tokens":577203,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2349},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01A28SaADC9yjzwAjitSLcMi":{"file_path":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md","content":"# Scoring and decision memory\n\nEvery decision (keep, reject with a reason, wishlist) is saved with **who** and **when**, together with how many customers asked at that moment. Later generations read this **decision memory**, so the AI does not push a request that was already rejected, unless the market has changed. The ranking rule and its weights are set by the team in **Dashboard → Settings** (`/dashboard/settings`).\n\n## The score (0–100, shown on every feature request)\n\n| Part | What it measures | Default weight |\n|---|---|---|\n| Demand | Customers asking in the chosen market, log-scaled against the top request | 60 % |\n| Market backing | Competitor features and trends (research agent) that support the request | 25 % |\n| Principle fit | The request's category matches the series' focus (BMW principles) | 15 % |\n\n```\nbase      = 100 × (wD·demand + wB·backing + wF·fit) / (wD + wB + wF)\nstrength  = 0.5 ^ (days since the decision / half-life)            default half-life 365 days\ngrowth    = (mentions now − mentions at decision) / mentions at decision\n\nrejected before:  score = base × (1 − penalty × strength)          default penalty 60 %\n   … unless growth ≥ resurface threshold → \"Resurfaced\", score = base   default +30 %\nkept before:      score = base + 10 × bonus × strength             default +5 points\noptional:         hide rejected requests instead of ranking them lower\nmemory scope:     same market (default) or all markets\n```\n\nThe PM's drag order always wins over the score. The score sets the default order and is shown so the PM can see why.\n\n## Flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  %% How past decisions shape the next generation.\n  classDef human fill:#fdecea,stroke:#e22718,color:#121722,stroke-width:2px\n  classDef store fill:#0f3d75,stroke:#0f3d75,color:#ffffff\n  classDef ai fill:#e8f0fc,stroke:#1c69d4,color:#121722\n  classDef cfg fill:#eef1f6,stroke:#5b6676,color:#121722\n\n  subgraph G1 [\"Generation 1\"]\n    pm1{{\"PM decides<br/>keep · reject + reason · wishlist\"}}:::human\n    d1[\"Decision<br/>by · role · at · reason · mentions_at\"]:::ai\n    pm1 --> d1\n  end\n\n  d1 --> mem[(\"Decision memory<br/>latest keep / reject per request<br/>(series + request; market or all)\")]:::store\n\n  subgraph G2 [\"Next generation\"]\n    reqs[\"New feature requests<br/>from fresh feedback + research\"]:::ai\n    match[\"Match to memory<br/>today: same series + title<br/>backend: + embedding similarity\"]:::ai\n    score[\"Dixi score<br/>demand · backing · fit<br/>× memory penalty / bonus\"]:::ai\n    list[\"Ranked list<br/>badges: Rejected · Resurfaced · Kept before\"]:::ai\n    pm2{{\"PM decides again<br/>sees the old reason, who and when\"}}:::human\n    reqs --> match --> score --> list --> pm2\n  end\n\n  mem --> match\n  settings[\"Settings<br/>weights · penalty · bonus · half-life<br/>resurface threshold · hide / rank lower\"]:::cfg --> score\n  pm2 --> mem\n```\n\n## Today vs backend\n\n| | Today (prototype, `web/`) | Backend (planned, `backend/`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Decisions | Saved with each generation in localStorage (`dixi:sessions`) | Table `decision` in Supabase, one row per decision, never overwritten |\n| Matching | Same series + same request title (`memoryKey`) | Same + pgvector similarity between a new cluster and past rejected requests, so a reworded request is still recognised |\n| Scoring | `web/src/lib/pipeline/scoring.ts` (`buildMemory`, `scoreRequest`) | Same rules in `backend/app/scoring/`, unit-tested against the web version |\n| Settings | `/dashboard/settings`, localStorage (`dixi:scoring`) | Table `scoring_settings` per team, with change history |\n| AI agent | Not involved yet: the list is built by a script | The requirement agent calls `get_decision_memory(series, market)` before it proposes requests. Rule in its instructions: *do not propose a rejected request again unless it resurfaced; when you do, quote the old reason and show the demand change.* |\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfuC2FjeXjC3je47znqNA","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f4391db9-e1d1-4915-a4c7-5d034a0513b6","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:31:08.053Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
