{"parentUuid":"e748cdd1-2373-4f67-a085-bad93aad6d3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuCPRrggfVqFv7qT46nr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tjio3QoJqKWywP9zLTSWGd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/architecture/07-pm-workflow.md'; s=open(p).read()\na='cover · at a glance · requirements matrix ■ □ vs other profiles<br/>'\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+'ⓘ trace per requirement: feedback → competitors/trends → decision (who · when · why) → profile<br/>',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nimport re\nm=re.search(r\"```mermaid\\n(.*?)```\",s,re.S).group(1)\nh=open('reports/pm-workflow.html').read()\nh=re.sub(r'<pre class=\"mermaid\">.*?</pre>', lambda _:'<pre class=\"mermaid\">'+m.replace(\"<\",\"&lt;\").replace(\">\",\"&gt;\")+'</pre>', h, flags=re.S)\nopen('reports/pm-workflow.html','w').write(h)\nEOF\nnode /Volumes/PJ/DevCache/claude-tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-PJ-peresjav-hackathons-ehl-final-minuch-2026/7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1/scratchpad/cdp-eval.mjs \"file://$PWD/reports/pm-workflow.html\" \"document.title\" 2 3000\ncat > prompts/26-decision-memory-scoring.md <<'EOF'\n# 26 · Decision memory, scoring algorithm, settings, trace (2026-10-10)\n\n> You need to update the architecture and make sure that the decision that has been made and these Comments and the decisions should be saved and then the AI should retrieve this information in the backend for upcoming generations so the AI don't suggest any feature that was already rejected in the past. So basically, these features should be scored or have a lower score, and then even if the market changes and then maybe this feature is more valuable in the future, then maybe it can hide or score in a higher position. So we should actually have a kind of algorithm for scoring this list and we have a weight for them. But this should be of course in the architecture and maybe in the settings of the dashboard.\n\n> why it's look like that [screenshot]? seems without info there.\n> there is one iisue in the page can you check it out\n> In the profile page we should see also the tracks of the decision. So maybe we can have a little icon of details that shows exactly from where it's coming this information.\n\n**Result:** lib/pipeline/scoring.ts (Dixi score = demand · market backing · principle fit; decision memory from earlier generations: reject penalty with half-life, \"resurfaced\" when demand grows ≥ threshold, keep bonus, hide option); decisions store mentionsAt; list ranked by score with Rejected / Resurfaced / Kept-before badges; /dashboard/settings with sliders + live example; matrix headers compacted (A/B/C); dev overlay checked across the full flow (no issues; settings Date.now fixed); ⓘ trace panel per requirement on the profile page. Docs: new 09-scoring-and-memory.md, 03/07/README/backend README updated.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Update diagram, validate, log prompt","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1910,"cache_read_input_tokens":590995,"output_tokens":1551,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":377},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1910,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1551,"cache_read_input_tokens":590995,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1910},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Tjio3QoJqKWywP9zLTSWGd":{"command":"cd /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026 && pyth