{"parentUuid":"51e7923a-58d9-4f27-8309-d19dd3f0c940","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","isWorktree":false,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":[],"platform":"darwin","shell":"zsh","osVersion":"Darwin 27.2.0","scratchpadDirectory":"/Volumes/PJ/DevCache/claude-tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-PJ-peresjav-hackathons-ehl-final-minuch-2026/7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1/scratchpad"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f8dd4191-b2b9-4bb1-9e80-72542c6ef23e","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:36:04.610Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026 (was /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"f8dd4191-b2b9-4bb1-9e80-72542c6ef23e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14949808 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"55ee9b6c-b437-4850-96e1-53f50dada124","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:36:04.610Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14949808 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"55ee9b6c-b437-4850-96e1-53f50dada124","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuCRRMjJsiBQRcfkGFvJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Rejected requests now lose priority in later generations unless demand grows, the weights are adjustable in a new Settings page, and the architecture docs describe it all. I tested it in a headless browser: the 5 Series request rejected in the first generation (\"Simpler iDrive menus and touchscreen\", 81 customers asking) came back last of 25 in the next analysis, with a red \"Rejected 10 Oct 2026\" badge and a score of 33 instead of about 80. Types and lint pass.\n\n**Decision memory and scoring**\n- **What's saved:** every keep and reject records who, their role, when, the reason, and how many customers were asking at that moment. Each build keeps a copy of its decisions as a generation.\n- **Next analysis:** for the same series (and the same market by default), Dixi reads those past decisions.\n  - **Score:** every feature request shows a score from 0 to 100, built from demand (60%), backing from competitors and trends (25%) and fit with BMW principles (15%). The score sets the default order; your drag order still wins.\n  - **Rejected before:** the score drops by 60% and the card shows a red \"Rejected <date>\" badge. The details panel shows who rejected it, when, why, and how many customers were asking then.\n  - **Fading:** the penalty halves every 365 days, so old rejects count less over time.\n  - **Resurfaced:** if demand has grown 30% or more since the reject, the penalty is lifted and an amber \"Resurfaced +X%\" badge appears.\n  - **Kept before:** a small bonus and a green badge.\n  - **Optional:** hide earlier rejects instead of ranking them lower.\n\n**Settings** (the sliders icon in the top bar, `/dashboard/settings`): sliders for the three weights, the reject penalty, the keep bonus, how fast decisions fade, and the resurfacing threshold. You can also choose same market or all markets, switch hiding on or off, and reset. A live example shows how one request scores in each situation, and the formula is written out.\n\n**Trace on the profile page:** each requirement in the requirements table has an **ⓘ** icon. It opens a side panel with the full path: customer feedback (mentions, channels) → competitors and trends behind it → the decision (who, role, when, why, priority, customers asking then) → placed in this profile. Below that are the evidence, sources, matching options and customer quotes. The icon is left out of the PDF.\n\n**Empty space in the table:** that came from the tall turned profile names in the header. The columns are now **A / B / C** with colour dots, and the full names are in a short key above the table.\n\n**The page issue:** I couldn't reproduce it. The Next.js overlay showed \"no issues\" at every step of a full run. It was most likely the Settings-page error I fixed during this work, which stays in the overlay until a reload. If you still see it after **Cmd+Shift+R**, send me a screenshot.\n\n**Architecture docs:**\n- **`09-scoring-and-memory.md` (new):** the formula, a diagram of how past decisions shape the next generation, and today versus the backend plan.\n  - In the backend, the AI agent calls `get_decision_memory(series, market)` before proposing requests. It doesn't re-propose a reject unless it resurfaced, and then it quotes the old reason.\n  - Matching will also use text similarity, so a reworded request is still recognised. Today it matches on the same series and the same request title.\n- **Also updated:** `03-data-model.md` (customers asking at decision time, scoring settings), `07-pm-workflow.md` (memory, score and settings feed the list, plus the trace icon), `docs/README.md`, and `backend/README.md` (decision memory listed as a must-have for the agents).\n\nEverything still lives in your browser until Supabase is connected. Still open: **three markets (Europe, China, USA), or the UK instead of Japan?**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1678,"cache_read_input_tokens":592905,"output_tokens":1275,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1678,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1275,"cache_read_input_tokens":592905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1678},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuCRNQsdKNfShZTyfCsi","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1566cff1-bbaa-4a0f-a636-64ed92902b1e","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:36:18.129Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
