{"parentUuid":"7b4bc89c-13a0-4a5b-ace5-30117cc6bc57","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web/src/lib/pipeline/posts.ts","snippet":"38\t  },\n39\t};\n40\t\n41\texport function buildPost(p: Profile, cfg: SeriesConfig, scopeLabel: string): Post {\n42\t  const story = STORY[p.id] ?? STORY.fix;\n43\t  const asks = p.requests.slice(0, 3).map((r) => lower(r.title));\n44\t  const wish = p.wishes[0];\n45\t  const caption = [\n46\t    `Drivers in ${scopeLabel === \"USA\" ? \"the USA\" : scopeLabel} ${story.open}: ${list(asks)}.`,\n47\t    story.close(cfg.name),\n48\t    wish ? `Inspired by what the market loves: ${lower(wish.title)}.` : \"\",\n49\t  ]\n50\t    .filter(Boolean)\n51\t    .join(\" \");\n52\t  return {\n53\t    profileId: p.id,\n54\t    image: `/images/posts/${cfg.id.toLowerCase()}-${p.id}.webp`,"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"165f7432-2e2d-4868-952b-f0886a4036e6","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:55:57.664Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web/src/lib/pipeline/posts.ts changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n38\t  },\n39\t};\n40\t\n41\texport function buildPost(p: Profile, cfg: SeriesConfig, scopeLabel: string): Post {\n42\t  const story = STORY[p.id] ?? STORY.fix;\n43\t  const asks = p.requests.slice(0, 3).map((r) => lower(r.title));\n44\t  const wish = p.wishes[0];\n45\t  const caption = [\n46\t    `Drivers in ${scopeLabel === \"USA\" ? \"the USA\" : scopeLabel} ${story.open}: ${list(asks)}.`,\n47\t    story.close(cfg.name),\n48\t    wish ? `Inspired by what the market loves: ${lower(wish.title)}.` : \"\",\n49\t  ]\n50\t    .filter(Boolean)\n51\t    .join(\" \");\n52\t  return {\n53\t    profileId: p.id,\n54\t    image: `/images/posts/${cfg.id.toLowerCase()}-${p.id}.webp`,\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"165f7432-2e2d-4868-952b-f0886a4036e6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14979328 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4af15e2f-5d09-4fcc-a1bd-b5591b714379","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:55:57.664Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14979328 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"4af15e2f-5d09-4fcc-a1bd-b5591b714379","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuDwKhNcVPDqt96PuEm4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Analytics page now shows one social post per profile, with an AI-generated image and a short story built from what customers in that market asked for. I tested it on a 7 Series USA generation and there were no errors.\n\n**What each post card shows:**\n- **Header:** the profile as the account, e.g. \"Tech-forward · Concept test · 7 Series · USA\", with a \"Best\" badge on the leader.\n- **Image:** a square scene with a headline over it and a visible **\"AI-generated image\"** label (EU AI Act).\n- **After the test:** likes, comments, shares and the share of positive reactions. Before the test, the posts appear as \"Ready to post\".\n- **Story and hashtags:** for example #Next7Series #Techforward #USA #ConceptTest.\n\n**How the story is written:** it names the problem customers told us about, then the feeling once it's solved, and closes with a wishlist item when the profile has one. Example for Fix the basics:\n> \"Drivers in the USA told us what gets in the way every morning: better phone connectivity (CarPlay, Bluetooth), stronger climate control with easy controls and faster, more stable infotainment. The next 7 Series fixes the basics first. No workarounds, no second tries: you get in, and it just works.\"\n\nEach profile has its own mood:\n\n| Profile | Headline | Scene |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fix the basics | \"Every drive starts calm.\" | Calm city sunrise, phone connecting on the charging pad, simple physical buttons |\n| Tech-forward | \"The road ahead, upgraded.\" | Night highway, glowing digital cockpit and driver assistance |\n| Comfort & craft | \"Arrive as rested as you left.\" | Golden hour, stitched leather, wood trim, panoramic roof |\n\n**The images:**\n- **What I made:** 9 images with your OpenAI key (3 series × 3 stories), in `web/public/images/posts/`. They cost about 440 output tokens each at medium quality.\n- **Rules:** no logos, badges, text, plates or faces; people appear only from behind. Each image has a file next to it recording the prompt, and the prompts are in `scripts/prompts/posts.json` so they can be regenerated.\n- **Comfort & craft:** the image model made these as four-panel collages, which reads like a carousel post. I kept them; I can regenerate them as single shots if you prefer.\n- **Fixed per car:** the image depends only on the series and the profile type, while the story text changes with the market and that generation's requests.\n\n**Still simulated:** no real posts are made and the reactions are not real; the page says so. With a real social channel connected, these numbers would come from actual posts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1380,"cache_read_input_tokens":615744,"output_tokens":873,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1380,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":873,"cache_read_input_tokens":615744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1380},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuDwKA8NPnoSP51Sdz7P","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5215c311-288d-4df9-a0d5-f3008d8c9151","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:56:06.562Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackatho