{"parentUuid":"a71bdb0b-e162-43ee-be2a-4f1ccbb420e5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuEXHiVxi9zBhBnW9GBv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VFeXACMEe7ezjJbtt5ghHx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026 && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert a in s,(p,a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('web/src/app/api/scoring-advice/route.ts',[('Change only what the manager\\'s instruction implies; keep everything else as in the current settings.','Change only what the manager\\'s instruction implies; keep everything else as in the current settings.\\nThe settings apply to every series and market. If the instruction names one series or market, say in the summary that the change applies to all of them.')])\ns=open('web/.env.example').read()\ns+='\\n# Server only (never NEXT_PUBLIC_): lets /api/scoring-advice turn a manager\\'s instruction into scoring settings.\\n# Locally the route also reads the repo-root .env. Without a key it falls back to simple keyword rules.\\nOPENAI_API_KEY=\\nOPENAI_MODEL_FAST=gpt-6-luna\\n'\nopen('web/.env.example','w').write(s)\n\nedit('docs/architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md',[\n ('''The PM's drag order always wins over the score.''','''## Tell Dixi in your words (natural-language settings)\n\nA manager can write the rule instead of moving sliders, e.g. *\"For the 7 Series, past rejects should count for two years and hardly ever come back.\"*\n\n1. The Settings page sends the text and the current settings to `POST /api/scoring-advice` (Next.js route handler, server only).\n2. The route asks an OpenAI model (`gpt-6-luna`, then fallbacks) for **typed JSON** (strict schema): the proposed settings, one plain sentence per change, and a summary. Without an API key (e.g. a public deployment) it uses simple keyword rules instead.\n3. Every value is **clamped** to its allowed range (`clampSettings`). The model cannot set anything outside the limits.\n4. The manager sees **Now → Proposed** for each changed setting and clicks **Apply** or **Discard**. Nothing changes without that click.\n5. Each applied change goes to a **change log**: the instruction, who (name and role), when, AI model or rules, and the changes. Today it lives in localStorage (`dixi:scoring-log`); in the backend it becomes table `scoring_change`.\n\nSettings apply to every series and market today. Per-series settings are a natural next step: one `scoring_settings` row per series.\n\nThe PM's drag order always wins over the score.'''),\n ('''  settings[\"Settings<br/>weights · penalty · bonus · half-life<br/>resurface threshold · hide / rank lower\"]:::cfg --> score''','''  nl[\"Manager writes the rule<br/>in plain words\"]:::human --> advice[\"/api/scoring-advice<br/>AI proposes typed settings<br/>clamped to limits\"]:::ai --> apply{{\"Apply or discard<br/>logged: who · when · instruction\"}}:::human --> settings\n  settings[\"Settings<br/>weights · penalty · bonus · half-life<br/>resurface threshold · hide / rank lower\"]:::cfg --> score'''),\n ('''| Settings | `/dashboard/settings`, localStorage (`dixi:scoring`) | Table `scoring_settings` per team, with change history |''','''| Settings | `/dashboard/settings`, localStorage (`dixi:scoring`); natural-language proposals via `/api/scoring-advice`; change log `dixi:scoring-log` | Tables `scoring_settings` (per team, later per series) and `scoring_change` (instruction, proposal, applied by, at) |'''),\n])\nedit('docs/architecture/06-web-app.md',[('''    R5[\"/dashboard/generations#id · one generation<br/>profiles · analytics · decisions\"]:::route''','''    R5[\"/dashboard/generations#id · one generation<br/>profiles · analytics · decisions\"]:::route\n    R6[\"/dashboard/settings · scoring + decision memory<br/>POST /api/scoring-advice (AI → typed settings)\"]:::route''')])\ns=open('docs/README.md').read()\ns=s.replace('weights set in Dashboard → Settings;','weights set in Dashboard → Settings, with sliders or in plain words (AI proposes, manager applies, change logged);',1)\nopen('docs/README.md','w').write(s)\ns=open('docs/requirements.md').read()\ns=s.replace(\"| [`web/.env.example`](../web/.env.example) | `web/.env.local` | Public values only: site URL, backend API URL, Supabase URL + publishable key |\",\"| [`web/.env.example`](../web/.env.example) | `web/.env.local` | Public values (site URL, backend API URL, Supabase URL + publishable key) and the server-only `OPENAI_API_KEY` for `/api/scoring-advice` |\",1)\nopen('docs/requirements.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\nS=/Volumes/PJ/DevCache/claude-tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-PJ-peresjav-hackathons-ehl-final-minuch-2026/7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1/scratchpad; for f in 06-web-app 09-scoring-and-memory; do python3 - \"$f\" \"$S\" <<'EOF'\nimport re,sys\nf,S=sys.argv[1],sys.argv[2]\ns=open(f'docs/architecture/{f}.md').read()\nm=re.search(r\"```mermaid\\n(.*?)```\",s,re.S).group(1)\nh=open('reports/pm-workflow.html').read()\nh=re.sub(r'<pre class=\"mermaid\">.*?</pre>', lambda _:'<pre class=\"mermaid\">'+m.replace(\"<\",\"&lt;\").replace(\">\",\"&gt;\")+'</pre>', h, flags=re.S)\nopen(f'{S}/v-{f}.html','w').write(h)\nEOF\nprintf \"%s: \" $f; node $S/cdp-eval.mjs \"file://$S/v-$f.html\" \"document.title+' '+document.getElementById('err').textContent.slice(0,200)\" 2 2500 | tail -1; done; cd web && pnpm exec tsc --noEmit && pnpm lint >/dev/null && echo TS-LINT-OK","description":"Update docs, env template; validate diagrams and code","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6894,"cache_read_input_tokens":641577,"output_tokens":2911,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":599},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"