4dad635f-8b2e-4361-92da-b2c046d2ff46","timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:04:04.681Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"4dad635f-8b2e-4361-92da-b2c046d2ff46","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b2a3b805-59b1-4072-b298-4407cedf470f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFeXACMEe7ezjJbtt5ghHx","type":"tool_result","content":"06-web-app: \"OK \"\n09-scoring-and-memory: \"OK \"\nTS-LINT-OK","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1bdef432-e936-4eec-8866-d9b7c08a4a20","timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:04:31.840Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"06-web-app: \"OK \"\n09-scoring-and-memory: \"OK \"\nTS-LINT-OK","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":15,"oldLines":7,"newStart":15,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | [`06-web-app.md`](architecture/06-web-app.md) | The current Next.js app: routes, components, shared globe, data modules, planned backend |"," | [`07-pm-workflow.md`](architecture/07-pm-workflow.md) | The product manager's path, as built in `/dashboard/[market]/[series]`: market → series → AI analysis + research agent (competitors, trends) → keep / reject with a required reason / reorder priority / wishlist → profiles that follow the PM's priority → optional social test (L3) |"," | [`08-decision-audit.md`](architecture/08-decision-audit.md) | How one decision is made and audited: reject → required reason → decision {by, at, reason} → decision log, profile decision trail, PDF → snapshot in the next generation |","-| [`09-scoring-and-memory.md`](architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md) | The Dixi score (demand · market backing · principle fit) and decision memory: past rejects lower a request in later generations, fading with a half-life, unless demand grew (\"resurfaced\"); weights set in Dashboard → Settings; backend plan for the AI agent |","+| [`09-scoring-and-memory.md`](architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md) | The Dixi score (demand · market backing · principle fit) and decision memory: past rejects lower a request in later generations, fading with a half-life, unless demand grew (\"resurfaced\"); weights set in Dashboard → Settings, with sliders or in plain words (AI proposes, manager applies, change logged); backend plan for the AI agent |"," "," ## Core ideas in one paragraph"," Dixi helps a BMW product manager turn what each market says into car profiles for the next 1, 5 or 7 Series, and keeps the reason for every decision. Inputs sit in three layers: **L1 BMW principles** (the fundamentals of each series, owned by managers), **L2 market evidence** (customer feedback and feature requests, customer studies, sales, today's option list, plus a research agent that adds competitor features people like and market trends, each with sources) and **L3 social test** (runs only after profiles exist: which profile tracks better on social media; low weight per series: 7 Series 2 %, 5 Series 8 %, 1 Series 20 %). The PM picks a market and a series; AI clusters the evidence into feature requests by category and urgency; the PM keeps or rejects each one (a reject needs a reason), drags them into priority order and wishlists competitor or trend features. Dixi then builds three profiles that follow that priority (score = L1 principles + priority fit, plus L2 coverage) and saves the build as a **generation** with its profiles, decisions and priority. Every decision records who made it (name and role, from a simple local identity until there is a login) and when, and shows up in the decision log, the profile's decision trail and its PDF. Today decisions, priority and generations live in the browser (localStorage); BMW-derived data stays local and git-ignored, and the public deployment runs on example data. Supabase tables are planned."]}]},{"filePath":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/06-web-app.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":6,"newStart":14,"newLines":7,"lines":["     R1[\"/ · landing\"]:::route","     R2[\"/dashboard · Generations (home)<br/>/dashboard/new · New analysis (globe)\"]:::route","     R5[\"/dashboard/generations#id · one generation<br/>profiles · analytics · decisions\"]:::route","+    R6[\"/dashboard/settings · scoring + decision memory<br/>POST /api/scoring-advice (AI → typed settings)\"]:::route","     R3[\"/dashboard/[market] · choose a series\"]:::route","     R4[\"/dashboard/[market]/[series] · requirement pipeline<br/>1-series · 5-series · 7-series\"]:::route","   end"]}]},{"filePath":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":22,"oldLines":6,"newStart":22,"newLines":18,"lines":[" memory scope:     same market (default) or all markets"," ```"," ","+## Tell Dixi in your words (natural-language settings)","+","+A manager can write the rule instead of moving sliders, e.g. *\"For the 7 Series, past rejects should count for two years and hardly ever come back.\"*","+","+1. The Settings page sends the text and the current settings to `POST /api/scoring-advice` (Next.js route handler, server only).","+2. The route asks an OpenAI model (`gpt-6-luna`, then fallbacks) for **typed JSON** (strict schema): the proposed settings, one plain sentence per change, and a summary. Without an API key (e.g. a public deployment) it uses simple keyword rules instead.","+3. Every value is **clamped** to its allowed range (`clampSettings`). The model cannot set anything outside the limits.","+4. The manager sees **Now → Proposed** for each changed setting and clicks **Apply** or **Discard**. Nothing changes without that click.","+5. Each applied change goes to a **change log**: the instruction, who (name and role), when, AI model or rules, and the changes. Today it lives in localStorage (`dixi:scoring-log`); in the backend it becomes table `scoring_change`.","+","+Settings apply to every series and market today. Per-series settings are a natural next step: one `scoring_settings` row per series.","+"," The PM's drag order always wins over the score. The score sets the default order and is shown so the PM can see why."," "," ## Flow"]},{"oldStart":52,"oldLines":6,"newStart":64,"newLines":7,"lines":["   end"," ","   mem --> match","+  nl[\"Manager writes the rule<br/>in plain words\"]:::human --> advice[\"/api/scoring-advice<br/>AI proposes typed settings<br/>clamped to limits\"]:::ai --> apply{{\"Apply or discard<br/>logged: who · when · instruction\"}}:::human --> settings","   settings[\"Settings<br/>weights · penalty · bonus · half-life<br/>resurface threshold · hide / rank lower\"]:::cfg --> score","   pm2 --> mem"," ```"]},{"oldStart":63,"oldLines":5,"newStart":76,"newLines":5,"lines":[" | Decisions | Saved with each generation in localStorage (`dixi:sessions`) | Table `decision` in Supabase, one row per decision, never overwritten |"," | Matching | Same series + same request title (`memoryKey`) | Same + pgvector similarity between a new cluster and past rejected requests, so a reworded request is still recognised |"," | Scoring | `web/src/lib/pipeline/scoring.ts` (`buildMemory`, `scoreRequest`) | Same rules in `backend/app/scoring/`, unit-tested against the web version |","-| Settings | `/dashboard/settings`, localStorage (`dixi:scoring`) | Table `scoring_settings` per team, with change history |","+| Settings | `/dashboard/settings`, localStorage (`dixi:scoring`); natural-language proposals via `/api/scoring-advice`; change log `dixi:scoring-log` | Tables `scoring_settings` (per team, later per series) and `scoring_change` (instruction, proposal, applied by, at) |"," | AI agent | Not involved yet: the list is built by a script | The requirement agent calls `get_decision_memory(series, market)` before it proposes requests. Rule in its instructions: *do not propose a rejected request again unless it resurfaced; when you do, quote the old reason and show the demand change.* |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/requirements.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":72,"oldLines":7,"newStart":72,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," | Template | Copy to | Contains |"," |---|---|---|","-| [`web/.env.example`](../web/.env.example) | `web/.env.local` | Public values only: site URL, backend API URL, Supabase URL + publishable key |","+| [`web/.env.example`](../web/.env.example) | `web/.env.local` | Public values (site URL, backend API URL, Supabase URL + publishable key) and the server-only `OPENAI_API_KEY` for `/api/scoring-advice` |"," | [`backend/.env.example`](../backend/.env.example) | `backend/.env` | Server secrets: OpenAI key and model names, Supabase service role key, database URL, CORS, optional Logfire / fal.ai keys |"," | — | repo-root `.env` | `OPENAI_API_KEY` for `scripts/generate-image.mjs` (optional `OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL`) |"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web/.env.example","hunks":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":3,"newStart":11,"newLines":8,"lines":[" # hosted values from the Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API."," NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321"," NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=","+","+# Server only (never NEXT_PUBLIC_): lets /api/scoring-advice turn a manager's instruction into scoring settings.","+# Locally the route also reads the repo-root .env. Without a key it falls back to simple keyword rules.","+OPENAI_API_KEY=","REDACTED"]}]}],"moreFiles":1,"changedFiles":["/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/README.md","/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/06-web-app.md","/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md","/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/requirements.md","/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web/.env.example","/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web/src/app/api/scoring-advice/route.ts"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4dad635f-8b2e-4361-92da-b2c046d2ff46","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"1bdef432-e936-4eec-8866-d9b7c08a4a20","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md","snippet":"17\t\n18\trejected before:  score = base × (1 − penalty × strength)          default penalty 60 %\n19\t   … unless growth ≥ resurface threshold → \"Resurfaced\", score = base   default +30 %\n20\tkept before:      score = base + 10 × bonus × strength             default +5 points\n21\toptional:         hide rejected requests instead of ranking them lower\n22\tmemory scope:     same market (default) or all markets\n23\t```\n24\t\n25\t## Tell Dixi in your words (natural-language settings)\n26\t\n27\tA manager can write the rule instead of moving sliders, e.g. *\"For the 7 Series, past rejects should count for two years and hardly ever come back.\"*\n28\t\n29\t1. The Settings page sends the text and the current settings to `POST /api/scoring-advice` (Next.js route handler, server only).\n30\t2. The route asks an OpenAI model (`gpt-6-luna`, then fallbacks) for **typed JSON** (strict schema): the proposed settings, one plain sentence per change, and a summary. Without an API key (e.g. a public deployment) it uses simple keyword rules instead.\n31\t3. Every value is **clamped** to its allowed range (`clampSettings`). The model cannot set anything outside the limits.\n32\t4. The manager sees **Now → Proposed** for each changed setting and clicks **Apply** or **Discard**. Nothing changes without that click.\n33\t5. Each applied change goes to a **change log**: the instruction, who (name and role), when, AI model or rules, and the changes. Today it lives in localStorage (`dixi:scoring-log`); in the backend it becomes table `scoring_change`.\n34\t\n35\tSettings apply to every series and market today. Per-series settings are a natural next step: one `scoring_settings` row per series.\n36\t\n37\tThe PM's drag order always wins over the score. The score sets the default order and is shown so the PM can see why.\n38\t\n39\t## Flow\n40\t\n41\t```mermaid\n42\tflowchart LR\n43\t  %% How past decisions shape the next generation.\n44\t  classDef human fill:#fdecea,stroke:#e22718,color:#121722,stroke-width:2px\n...\n47\t    match[\"Match to memory<br/>today: same series + title<br/>backend: + embedding similarity\"]:::ai\n48\t    score[\"Dixi score<br/>demand · backing · fit<br/>× memory penalty / bonus\"]:::ai\n49\t    list[\"Ranked list<br/>badges: Rejected · Resurfaced · Kept before\"]:::ai\n50\t    pm2{{\"PM decides again<br/>sees the old reason, who and when\"}}:::human\n51\t    reqs --> match --> score --> list --> pm2\n52\t  end\n53\t\n54\t  mem --> match\n55\t  nl[\"Manager writes the rule<br/>in plain words\"]:::human --> advice[\"/api/scoring-advice<br/>AI proposes typed settings<br/>clamped to limits\"]:::ai --> apply{{\"Apply or discard<br/>logged: who · when · instruction\"}}:::human --> settings\n56\t  settings[\"Settings<br/>weights · penalty · bonus · half-life<br/>resurface threshold · hide / rank lower\"]:::cfg --> score\n57\t  pm2 --> mem\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t## Today vs backend\n61\t\n62\t| | Today (prototype, `web/`) | Backend (planned, `backend/`) |\n63\t|---|---|---|\n64\t| Decisions | Saved with each generation in localStorage (`dixi:sessions`) | Table `decision` in Supabase, one row per decision, never overwritten |\n65\t| Matching | Same series + same request title (`memoryKey`) | Same + pgvector similarity between a new cluster and past rejected requests, so a reworded request is still recognised |\n66\t| Scoring | `web/src/lib/pipeline/scoring.ts` (`buildMemory`, `scoreRequest`) | Same rules in `backend/app/scoring/`, unit-tested against the web version |\n67\t| Settings | `/dashboard/settings`, localStorage (`dixi:scoring`); natural-language proposals via `/api/scoring-advice`; change log `dixi:scoring-log` | Tables `scoring_settings` (per team, later per series) and `scoring_change` (instruction, proposal, applied by, at) |\n68\t| AI agent | Not involved yet: the list is built by a script | The requirement agent calls `get_decision_memory(series, market)` before it proposes requests. Rule in its instructions: *do not propose a rejected request again unless it resurfaced; when you do, quote the old reason and show the demand change.* |"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3de15880-b9ae-4044-bceb-66f8a4533622","timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:04:31.876Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/docs/architecture/09-scoring-and-memory.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n17\t\n18\trejected before:  score = base × (1 − penalty × strength)          default penalty 60 %\n19\t   … unless growth ≥ resurface threshold → \"Resurfaced\", score = base   default +30 %\n20\tkept before:      score = base + 10 × bonus × strength             default +5 points\n21\toptional:         hide rejected requests instead of ranking them lower\n22\tmemory scope:     same market (default) or all markets\n23\t```\n24\t\n25\t## Tell Dixi in your words (natural-language settings)\n26\t\n27\tA manager can write the rule instead of moving sliders, e.g. *\"For the 7 Series, past rejects should count for two years and hardly ever come back.\"*\n28\t\n29\t1. The Settings page sends the text and the current settings to `POST /api/scoring-advice` (Next.js route handler, server only).\n30\t2. The route asks an OpenAI model (`gpt-6-luna`, then fallbacks) for **typed JSON** (strict schema): the proposed settings, one plain sentence per change, and a summary. Without an API key (e.g. a public deployment) it uses simple keyword rules instead.\n31\t3. Every value is **clamped** to its allowed range (`clampSettings`). The model cannot set anything outside the limits.\n32\t4. The manager sees **Now → Proposed** for each changed setting and clicks **Apply** or **Discard**. Nothing changes without that click.\n33\t5. Each applied change goes to a **change log**: the instruction, who (name and role), when, AI model or rules, and the changes. Today it lives in localStorage (`dixi:scoring-log`); in the backend it becomes table `scoring_change`.\n34\t\n35\tSettings apply to every series and market today. Per-series settings are a natural next step: one `scoring_settings` row per series.\n36\t\n37\tThe PM's drag order always wins over the score. The score sets the default order and is shown so the PM can see why.\n38\t\n39\t## Flow\n40\t\n41\t```mermaid\n42\tflowchart LR\n43\t  %% How past decisions shape the next generation.\n44\t  classDef human fill:#fdecea,stroke:#e22718,color:#121722,stroke-width:2px\n...\n47\t    match[\"Match to memory<br/>today: same series + title<br/>backend: + embedding similarity\"]:::ai\n48\t    score[\"Dixi score<br/>demand · backing · fit<br/>× memory penalty / bonus\"]:::ai\n49\t    list[\"Ranked list<br/>badges: Rejected · Resurfaced · Kept before\"]:::ai\n50\t    pm2{{\"PM decides again<br/>sees the old reason, who and when\"}}:::human\n51\t    reqs --> match --> score --> list --> pm2\n52\t  end\n53\t\n54\t  mem --> match\n55\t  nl[\"Manager writes the rule<br/>in plain words\"]:::human --> advice[\"/api/scoring-advice<br/>AI proposes typed settings<br/>clamped to limits\"]:::ai --> apply{{\"Apply or discard<br/>logged: who · when · instruction\"}}:::human --> settings\n56\t  settings[\"Settings<br/>weights · penalty · bonus · half-life<br/>resurface threshold · hide / rank lower\"]:::cfg --> score\n57\t  pm2 --> mem\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t## Today vs backend\n61\t\n62\t| | Today (prototype, `web/`) | Backend (planned, `backend/`) |\n63\t|---|---|---|\n64\t| Decisions | Saved with each generation in localStorage (`dixi:sessions`) | Table `decision` in Supabase, one row per decision, never overwritten |\n65\t| Matching | Same series + same request title (`memoryKey`) | Same + pgvector similarity between a new cluster and past rejected requests, so a reworded request is still recognised |\n66\t| Scoring | `web/src/lib/pipeline/scoring.ts` (`buildMemory`, `scoreRequest`) | Same rules in `backend/app/scoring/`, unit-tested against the web version |\n67\t| Settings | `/dashboard/settings`, localStorage (`dixi:scoring`); natural-language proposals via `/api/scoring-advice`; change log `dixi:scoring-log` | Tables `scoring_settings` (per team, later per series) and `scoring_change` (instruction, proposal, applied by, at) |\n68\t| AI agent | Not involved yet: the list is built by a script | The requirement agent calls `get_decision_memory(series, market)` before it proposes requests. Rule in its instructions: *do not propose a rejected request again unless it resurfaced; when you do, quote the old reason and show the demand change.* |\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026/web","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
