{"parentUuid":"8a3a3696-27b7-41af-b974-bc2263c089a5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuKehRJxY7mb3QUksQq7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2614,"cache_read_input_tokens":688807,"output_tokens":1628,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":445},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2614,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1628,"cache_read_input_tokens":688807,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2614},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11434,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuKegs4y5ZZoBMoonUBG","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5637a917-3c38-4bda-9187-fcd35decdeba","timestamp":"2026-10-10T22:11:05.712Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"5637a917-3c38-4bda-9187-fcd35decdeba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuKehRJxY7mb3QUksQq7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly yes. Usually one trail is tied to one branch, you review and approve on entire.io, and a GitHub PR runs underneath for CI. Runners are AI reviewers that check every push. This comes from Entire's trails guide (September 2026) in your sources and the runner configs in `.entire/runners/`.\n\n**Trail = branch?** Usually, but not always.\n- A trail can start **without a branch**, at the idea stage, with just a description of the problem and the intended solution. That's what we just created (trail 1).\n- Once there's code, a trail is normally linked to **one branch**: a new one, or an existing one you pick. You commit and push to that branch, and Entire attaches the commits, checkpoints and agent sessions to the trail.\n\n**Where does approval happen?** On entire.io, with a GitHub PR underneath.\n- The guide says: *\"Each Trail is currently backed by a PR on GitHub for CI.\"* So a PR exists, but mainly so GitHub can run checks.\n- **The review flow is on the trail page:**\n  - Read the description.\n  - Check the monitors (Confidence, Risk, Security, Drift).\n  - View the diff.\n  - Fix, resolve or dismiss findings.\n  - Click **Approve**, then **Merge**.\n- **Merge gates** (set by the repo owner in Settings → Gates) decide whether Merge is allowed:\n\n| Gate | What it checks |\n|---|---|\n| Up to date | The branch is current with its base |\n| Human review | Approvals on the **Trail**: minimum count, whether the author counts, whether new pushes reset approvals |\n| Agent review | No unresolved runner findings on the latest push (from a minimum severity) |\n| Checks | CI checks reported through GitHub |\n\n  Someone can be allowed to bypass a blocking gate, and every bypass is recorded on the trail.\n- **Approving the PR on GitHub:** the guide lists only approvals on the trail under human review, so I wouldn't count on a GitHub approval satisfying that gate.\n\n**What the runners do:** they're automatic AI reviewers that run on every push to a trail branch (when \"Auto build on push\" is on). Your repo has the 6 defaults:\n\n| Runner | What it produces |\n|---|---|\n| **Trail Review** | Findings on the diff against the base branch: only real bugs, regressions, security issues or data-loss risks, each with a severity. These feed the \"Agent review\" gate |\n| **Trail Summary** | A summary of what changed |\n| **Risk**, **Confidence**, **Security**, **Drift** | The monitor scores on the trail page. Drift likely shows how far the code moved from the trail description (inferred from the name) |\n\nEach runner is Claude (Sonnet) in a sandbox with **read-only** access to the repo and a 15-minute limit, set in `.entire/runners/trail-review.json`. You can change these settings or the instructions in those files.\n\n**Why our trail has no branch:** all the work went straight to `main`, so there was nothing for a trail to review. From now on:\n1. `entire trail create --title \"…\" --checkout`: creates the trail and switches to its new branch.\n2. Work and commit as usual.\n3. Push: the runners review it, the trail shows the findings and scores.\n4. Approve and Merge on entire.io: the change lands on `main`, and Vercel deploys it.\n\nStill open from before: should I delete the empty branch `dixi-mvp-requirement-pipeline-generations-and-decision-memory` that the failed attempts pushed (it's identical to `main`)?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2614,"cache_read_input_tokens":688807,"output_tokens":1628,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":445},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2614,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1628,"cache_read_input_tokens":688807,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2614},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfuKegs4y5ZZoBMoonUBG","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba18ad8b-cb16-4ef1-a1f4-0fa6e46717bf","timestamp":"2026-10-10T22:11:10.151Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
