{"parentUuid":"5558fe94-c4a8-4645-b915-a9945457f210","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuLCqsSxq7a187BW8Dc5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_read_input_tokens":697523,"output_tokens":1531,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":415},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1531,"cache_read_input_tokens":697523,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11138,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuLCqRu3agVKztqKTrSt","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"35e9292a-eb84-4f57-96a4-6452f6ea25b5","timestamp":"2026-10-10T22:18:21.432Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
{"parentUuid":"35e9292a-eb84-4f57-96a4-6452f6ea25b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuLCqsSxq7a187BW8Dc5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Entire already keeps the \"why\" behind every line: each commit carries an `Entire-Checkpoint` link to the prompt and session that produced it, so intent survives as long as that link survives the merge. How useful it is depends on how small the commits are. Two tests on our repo showed both sides:\n\n**`entire search`: finding the reasoning (worked well).** I asked *\"why rejected features get a lower score in later generations\"*. It returned the right session, with the exact planning text (\"every past keep and reject, with its reason, person, date…\") and the commit `6a1399d`. It matches by meaning and by keywords across sessions, commits and checkpoints. You can filter, for example `author:`, `date:week`, `branch:`.\n\n**`entire why <file>:<line>`: who wrote this line and why (weak here).** For `scoring.ts:41` (`rejectPenalty: 0.6`) it found the right commit, checkpoint and session. But the prompt it showed was one of the first in this session (\"no, dont push to entire please…\"), and it warned it was *\"a best-effort guess\"*. The cause is our workflow, not Entire: four hours of work in one session became **one big commit**, so it can't tell which instruction produced which line.\n\n**How to use it for better decisions:**\n1. **One intent → one trail → one branch → small commits.** Then `why` points to the exact prompt behind a line, the trail holds the description, review findings, approvals and sessions, and search results are precise.\n2. **Write the intent into the trail description** (problem, intended outcome, constraints). That's what the Drift runner compares the code against, and what a reviewer reads before the diff.\n3. **Before changing code you don't understand**, run `entire why <file>:<line>`, then `entire checkpoint explain <id>` for the full context. `AGENTS.md` already tells agents to do this, so Claude or Codex will look up the reasoning before \"fixing\" something that was deliberate.\n4. **Before a new feature**, search for earlier attempts or rejects, e.g. `entire search \"physical climate buttons\"`, so you don't repeat a discussion that was already settled. It's the same idea as Dixi's decision memory, but for code decisions instead of product decisions.\n\n**Does intent survive a merge?**\n- **What survives a normal merge:** checkpoint links live in each commit's message, and the checkpoints are pushed to GitHub, so after a merge the commits arrive on `main` with their links intact.\n- **What I'm not sure about:** whether Entire's own Merge button squashes commits, and whether a squash keeps every checkpoint link. The guide doesn't say.\n- **How to check after the first merge:** run `entire why` on a merged line. If it shows the right prompt and session, the trail's intent survived.\n- The trail page itself stays on entire.io after merging, with description, findings, approvals and sessions, so the decision record isn't lost either way.\n\n**A link between Dixi and Entire:** when you build a Dixi requirement as code, put the Dixi generation and decision ID (e.g. `G-MV2UB4CN`, \"Higher-quality interior finish, kept by Marco Rossi\") in the trail description. Then a line of code traces back through the trail to the product decision and the customer comments behind it.\n\nThe offer from before still stands: I can run one real trail (the small docs update about session upload) so you can see the runners, `why` and merge in action. Say go."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_read_input_tokens":697523,"output_tokens":1531,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":415},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1531,"cache_read_input_tokens":697523,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfuLCqRu3agVKztqKTrSt","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f9ad5043-e64a-4eb8-9c3f-ec2d84ef9759","timestamp":"2026-10-10T22:18:26.270Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"53e0d48f-0e86-4176-8390-70cad3fe3f46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/PJ/peresjav/hackathons/ehl-final-minuch-2026","sessionId":"7fd52f13-5d0c-4e7f-8ec6-8a947b2499a1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"federated-petting-ripple"}
